# 🔹 Difference Between Promise and Async/Await

| Feature              | Promise         | Async/Await        |
| -------------------- | --------------- | ------------------ |
| Introduced           | ES6             | ES8                |
| Syntax               | .then().catch() | try/catch          |
| Readability          | Hard            | Easy               |
| Looks like           | Chain code      | Normal code        |
| Debugging            | Difficult       | Easy               |
| Error handling       | Separate catch  | Normal catch block |
| Interview preference | Less            | More               |
| Internally           | Base concept    | Built on promises  |

---

## Example Difference

### Promise Style

```js
loginUser()
.then(user => getOrders(user.id))
.then(orders => getProducts(orders))
.then(products => console.log(products))
.catch(err => console.log(err));
```

Hard to read ❌

---

### Async/Await Style

async function process() {
    try {
        const user = await loginUser();
        const orders = await getOrders(user.id);
        const products = await getProducts(orders);
        console.log(products);
    } catch (err) {
        console.log(err);
    }
}


Clean and readable ✅
